    "turns": [
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "Why does Whisper deserve its own place in the history of artificial intelligence?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial-hook"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "Before Whisper, strong speech recognizers were often optimized for specific languages, domains or curated datasets. The 2022 work tested whether a much larger and more diverse weakly supervised corpus could trade benchmark specialization for broad robustness.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-whisper-paper", "source-primary-record"],
            "claimIds": [
                "claim-annual-membership",
                "claim-publication-record",
                "claim-contributor-record",
                "claim-core-method",
                "claim-historical-significance"
            ],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.historical-background"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "Whisper uses an encoder-decoder Transformer and represents transcription, translation, language identification and timestamps in one sequence-to-sequence format. Training on 680,000 hours lets one model reuse signals across languages and tasks instead of maintaining separate pipelines.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-whisper-paper", "source-primary-record"],
            "claimIds": [
                "claim-annual-membership",
                "claim-publication-record",
                "claim-contributor-record",
                "claim-core-method",
                "claim-historical-significance"
            ],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.core-idea"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "Experts generally treat Whisper as a turning point in open, general-purpose speech recognition because its released models made robust multilingual transcription widely accessible. Its influence also extends to speech interfaces for later multimodal and conversational systems.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-whisper-paper", "source-primary-record"],
            "claimIds": [
                "claim-annual-membership",
                "claim-publication-record",
                "claim-contributor-record",
                "claim-core-method",
                "claim-historical-significance"
            ],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.long-term-legacy"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "As today's systems grow larger, which lessons from Whisper still matter, and which limits deserve to be questioned again?",
            "sourceIds": [
                "source-primary-record",
                "source-openalex-record",
                "source-benchcouncil-annual",
